<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mexican–American War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1846">1846</a>–<a href="/years/1848">1848</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Mexican-American War, Mexican War, United States–Mexican War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mexican–American War was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> from 1846 to 1848, following the American annexation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> and a border dispute. American forces occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> in 1847. By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-guadalupe-hidalgo">Treaty of Guadalupe Hidalgo</a> Mexico ceded about half its territory, including California and much of the American Southwest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mexican-american-war.jpg" alt="Mexican–American War" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adolphe Jean-Baptiste Bayot / Carl Nebel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nebel_Mexican_War_12_Scott_in_Mexico_City_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Those claims, inherited by the United States, led to the <b>Mexican–American War</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-texas">Republic of Texas · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Mexican–American War</b> of 1846–1848 added California and the Southwest.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-states">United States · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>At the time the anthem was written, Mexico was still feeling the effects of its bitter defeat in the <b>Mexican–American War</b>, in which it had ceded more than half of its territory to the United States, and the country was demoralised and divided.</blockquote><a href="/songs/himno-nacional-mexicano">Mexican National Anthem</a></li><li><blockquote>The annexation helped provoke the <b>Mexican-American War</b> the following year.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-29">29 December in history</a></li><li><blockquote>His first company failed, but orders during the <b>Mexican-American War</b> made Colt revolvers famous worldwide.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/february-25">25 February in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Washington Allon Bartlett's proclamation renaming Yerba Buena as San Francisco took effect, months after US forces raised the American flag there in the <b>Mexican–American War</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-30">30 January in history</a></li></ul></section>
